# Build context for apps/api/Dockerfile is the REPO ROOT (the image needs
# pnpm-workspace.yaml, the root package.json and prisma/), so this file is what
# stops that from meaning "upload the whole working tree".
#
# Excluding .git is not cosmetic: it is the largest thing here and it carries
# every secret that has ever been committed and reverted. A build context is a
# tarball sent to a daemon — treat it like a diff.

.git
.github
.husky
.turbo
node_modules
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.next
**/.turbo

# Never in an image. .env holds the local Meta secrets (runbook: whatsapp-sandbox)
# and staging reads its own from Secrets Manager at task start (Gov §11.5).
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# NOT excluded, and this trips people: apps/web, e2e, evals, packages/* and
# services/* are pnpm workspace members (pnpm-workspace.yaml). Dropping any of
# their package.json files makes `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` fail with a
# lockfile-mismatch error that says nothing about the missing directory. They
# contribute a few KB of manifests; only their node_modules are excluded above.
docs
infra

**/*.log
**/.DS_Store
